# Keeps the build context small and keeps secrets out of every image layer. The Dockerfile installs
# dependencies itself (deps stage) and runs `next build`, so none of the host's build output is needed.

# Secrets: real .env files must never reach an image layer. Next's standalone output copies a .env it finds
# in the build context into the final image, so this is not only about the builder stage. The build does not
# read .env.example, so nothing is kept.
**/.env*

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image (host node_modules may even be for another OS)
**/node_modules
.next
.pnpm-store
out
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Local uploads (S3 or ephemeral disk in production)
media

# Repository and editor files
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
*.pem
*.log
